---
# Repo-root bundler config — the ONE vendor tree every app root shares.
#
# Committed on purpose, exactly like deployment/.bundle/config. BUNDLE_PATH is relative to
# each bundler app root, and this repo has two of them (here, and deployment/ — fastlane
# resolves lanes from a `fastlane/` subdirectory of cwd). deployment/ points at `../vendor/bundle`;
# this one points at the same tree from the root's own perspective, so `bundle install` from
# EITHER root materializes the identical 135M gem set ONCE instead of two copies that drift.
#
# Untracked, this fixes only the machine that wrote it: a fresh clone gets no `path` setting at
# all, root `bundle install` scatters gems into the global gem dir, and the two roots diverge
# again — the same defect in a new location. Asserted by RT-6 in
# scripts/product-health/checks/ruby-toolchain-coherence.sh.
#
# NOTE (CI): ruby/setup-ruby with `bundler-cache: true` runs `bundle config set --local path
# <cwd>/vendor/bundle` and OVERWRITES the app-root config it runs in. CI therefore ignores these
# values by design — it has only ever one bundler root per job (`working-directory: deployment`),
# so there is nothing to deduplicate there. This file is a local-development invariant. The thing
# that DOES matter in CI is asserted by RT-7.
BUNDLE_PATH: "vendor/bundle"
